<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Open Notes – Lfs</title><link>https://nagarajrpoojari.github.io/opennotes/tags/lfs/</link><description>Recent content in Lfs on Open Notes</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 01 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://nagarajrpoojari.github.io/opennotes/tags/lfs/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>x-Linux: Custom Linux Operating System Distribution</title><link>https://nagarajrpoojari.github.io/opennotes/projects/x-linux/</link><pubDate>Fri, 01 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://nagarajrpoojari.github.io/opennotes/projects/x-linux/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/nagarajpoojari404/x-Linux" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;View on GitHub&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="#the-build-pipeline"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Pipeline&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="#building-and-booting"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quickstart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;x-Linux&lt;/strong&gt; is an independent, custom Linux distribution and automated build orchestration pipeline designed following the &lt;strong&gt;Linux From Scratch (LFS)&lt;/strong&gt; methodology. It demonstrates how to bootstrap a minimal, self-contained, POSIX-compliant operating system directly from upstream source packages without relying on third-party precompiled binaries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="the-build-pipeline"&gt;The Build Pipeline&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="the-build-pipeline"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#the-build-pipeline" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div role="img" aria-label="Diagram"&gt;
&lt;pre class="mermaid hx:mt-6"&gt;
flowchart TD
Host[&amp;#34;Host Linux Machine&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; Phase1[&amp;#34;Phase 1: Cross-Toolchain Bootstrapping&amp;#34;]
Phase1 --&amp;gt; Toolchain[&amp;#34;Binutils, GCC, Glibc, Linux Headers&amp;#34;]
Toolchain --&amp;gt; Phase2[&amp;#34;Phase 2: Chroot Environment Setup&amp;#34;]
Phase2 --&amp;gt; Phase3[&amp;#34;Phase 3: Core System Software Compilation&amp;#34;]
Phase3 --&amp;gt; CoreLibs[&amp;#34;Bash, Coreutils, Systemd, Util-Linux, Grep&amp;#34;]
CoreLibs --&amp;gt; Phase4[&amp;#34;Phase 4: Linux Kernel Compilation&amp;#34;]
Phase4 --&amp;gt; Kernel[&amp;#34;Monolithic Custom Kernel (vmlinuz)&amp;#34;]
Kernel --&amp;gt; Phase5[&amp;#34;Phase 5: Initramfs, Bootloader &amp;amp; ISO Packaging&amp;#34;]
Phase5 --&amp;gt; Bootable[&amp;#34;Bootable Live ISO Image&amp;#34;]
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="key-system-components"&gt;Key System Components&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="key-system-components"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#key-system-components" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Toolchain Bootstrapping&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compiles a sanitized host-independent cross-compiler (&lt;code&gt;binutils&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;gcc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;glibc&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Isolates the build process using &lt;code&gt;chroot&lt;/code&gt; to ensure zero host-system contamination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Utilities &amp;amp; Shell&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds standard GNU userland tools (&lt;code&gt;bash&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;coreutils&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;findutils&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;grep&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;sed&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;tar&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;gzip&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;kmod&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configures user authentication, PAM, and basic networking utilities (&lt;code&gt;iproute2&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Linux Kernel Customization&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailored monolithic kernel configuration stripped of unneeded drivers for ultra-fast boot times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built-in ext4/FAT32 filesystem drivers, USB mass storage support, and EFI stub loader.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bootloader &amp;amp; Storage Layout&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GRUB2 bootloader installation supporting both legacy BIOS (MBR) and modern UEFI (GPT) boot modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bootable ISO generator for live testing in QEMU, VirtualBox, or physical bare-metal hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="building-and-booting"&gt;Building and Booting&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="building-and-booting"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#building-and-booting" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 data-hextra-search-id="requirements"&gt;Requirements&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="requirements"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#requirements" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Linux host machine (Debian/Ubuntu, Arch, or Fedora)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 16 GB free disk space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Root/sudo privileges for mount and chroot operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;QEMU (optional, for virtual machine testing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-hextra-search-id="automated-build-script"&gt;Automated Build Script&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="automated-build-script"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#automated-build-script" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Clone the build scripts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;git clone https://github.com/nagarajpoojari404/x-Linux.git
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; x-Linux
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Run the complete build and packaging pipeline&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;chmod +x build.sh
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;sudo ./build.sh&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
